<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rong people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rong, Xirong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rong were peoples of the western and northern borderlands of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> whom the Zhou states regarded as outsiders. Living in the uplands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a>, some were herders and others farmers in walled towns. One group, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanrong">Quanrong</a>, sacked the Western Zhou capital in 771 BCE, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> spent centuries fighting and absorbing Rong groups such as the Yiqu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rong-people.jpg" alt="Rong people" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philg88 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huaxiasiyi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
